# TEMPORARY — scanner limitation, not accepted product risk (except the
# RUNTIME section at the end).
#
# All entries above the RUNTIME section are devDependencies (build/test
# tooling) that never ship in the runtime bundle. Trivy fails to exclude dev dependencies for this repo:
# the yarn workspace walker aborts on wildcard version specs
# ("@types/node": "*", requested by vitest and @jest/types) and then counts
# every devDependency as production-reachable. Reproduced with trivy v0.73.0:
# WARN [yarn] Unable to parse package.json to remove dev dependencies
#   err="unable to resolve workspace dependencies: ... unable to match version
#   for @types/node"
#
# Remove this file once trivy's dev-dependency classification handles wildcard
# specs in yarn workspaces — the gate should then report these as dev-only on
# its own. Re-verify with: trivy fs . (warning "Unable to parse package.json to
# remove dev dependencies" must be gone).

# vite (build tool; fix requires a 4.x -> 5.x+ major upgrade)
CVE-2024-52011
CVE-2026-53571
# vite dev-server open-in-editor endpoint (4.x direct, 5.x via vitest 0.34);
# the dev server binds to localhost only; fix requires 6.4.4+
CVE-2026-112942
# vitest (test runner, workspace devDep)
CVE-2026-47429
# tinypool (vitest 0.33/0.34 worker pool; options come from our own test
# config; fix requires tinypool 2.x, i.e. a vitest major upgrade)
CVE-2026-104848
CVE-2026-104849
# playwright (via @storybook/test-runner)
CVE-2025-59288
# tmp (via @lingui/cli -> inquirer -> external-editor)
CVE-2026-44705
CVE-2026-49982
# glob (lingui/storybook toolchains)
CVE-2025-64756
# minimatch (pinned exact by @microsoft/api-extractor)
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904
# brace-expansion (under minimatch 9 in dev toolchains)
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUNTIME — accepted risk, ships in the browser bundle (not a dev dependency).

# decode-uri-component 0.2.2 (via query-string 7 in
# @beda.software/fhir-questionnaire and sdc-qrf): quadratic CPU on malformed
# percent-encoded input. It runs client-side on the user's own URL, so a crafted
# link can only slow that browser tab. No fixed 0.2.x exists and the ESM-only
# 0.5.1 can't be forced under query-string 7's require(); remove once both
# packages move to query-string 8+ and decode-uri-component is pinned to 0.5.1.
CVE-2026-118664
